# >>> naming block - generated by "generate.sh --refresh-names", do not edit by hand
#
# ClangSharp matches these on exact names only, so every type is listed. Refresh it
# after changing the traversed headers; a normal run fails if any type is left in a
# .Generated namespace, which is what catches a new one arriving without an entry.
#
# Enum members keep the upstream spelling where that IS the idiomatic name - a pixel
# format is I420 - and are Pascal-cased where the member names a state, mode or flag.
#
# Absent is what cannot be generated: SpaPodPropFlag, SpaDataFlag and the PW_KEY_*
# strings are #define macros, and macro binding generation is fatal on this header set.

